1
00:00:05,737 --> 00:00:07,300
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,325 --> 00:00:08,885
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:10,741 --> 00:00:12,843
(Episode 31)

4
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:15,212
(Suragan Side Dishes)

5
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,783
I was going to surprise her.

6
00:00:45,468 --> 00:00:47,908
The number you dialed is not available.
Forwarding your call to voicemail...

7
00:00:53,284 --> 00:00:54,318
Chef.

8
00:00:56,086 --> 00:00:58,191
- Hello.
- Hello.

9
00:00:58,389 --> 00:01:01,025
I think you should find
Ms. Han Gyu Rim right away.

10
00:01:01,111 --> 00:01:02,248
What?

11
00:01:03,294 --> 00:01:05,007
Did something happen to Gyu Rim?

12
00:01:05,462 --> 00:01:06,554
Excuse me.

13
00:01:11,388 --> 00:01:13,437
What did you do to Gyu Yeong?

14
00:01:14,698 --> 00:01:16,502
Hey, move.

15
00:01:27,551 --> 00:01:29,486
The coffee spilled all of a sudden.

16
00:01:30,074 --> 00:01:32,343
I think I barely clipped you.

17
00:01:33,450 --> 00:01:35,900
Last time, you tried to hit me
with your car on purpose!

18
00:01:37,334 --> 00:01:39,190
Are you a psychopath or something?

19
00:01:40,764 --> 00:01:43,267
I asked you, what did you do to my sister?

20
00:01:45,925 --> 00:01:50,447
Hey, I really didn't do anything.

21
00:01:51,075 --> 00:01:55,012
Even when your sister deserved to get hit,
I held back time and time again!

22
00:01:55,405 --> 00:01:57,140
You really are a psycho.

23
00:01:58,515 --> 00:02:00,317
You're not normal!

24
00:02:01,191 --> 00:02:02,292
You're not going anywhere!

25
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:04,655
What else are you planning
to do to my sister?

26
00:02:07,051 --> 00:02:09,157
You're not going anywhere, you jerk!

27
00:02:09,552 --> 00:02:11,930
Move! Please, get out of the way!

28
00:02:12,142 --> 00:02:13,439
I have to go.

29
00:02:13,464 --> 00:02:14,898
- Move, please!
- No!

30
00:02:15,252 --> 00:02:17,898
I'll go. You stay home.

31
00:02:18,628 --> 00:02:21,514
That jerk told me to come without you.

32
00:02:21,672 --> 00:02:23,382
I'm the one who has to go!

33
00:02:23,407 --> 00:02:25,709
What on earth are you two doing?

34
00:02:26,076 --> 00:02:30,442
That whole amnesia act
and all your foolish behavior,

35
00:02:30,501 --> 00:02:32,668
were you just playing me?

36
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:34,385
Did you plan it together?

37
00:02:34,518 --> 00:02:36,420
What? The hemorrhoids?

38
00:02:37,087 --> 00:02:39,510
I'm sorry, Su Nam. I was wrong.

39
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:42,492
You can kill me when I get back,

40
00:02:42,753 --> 00:02:44,700
but please let me go for now.

41
00:02:44,827 --> 00:02:48,283
If I don't leave now,
Han Gyu Rim could get hurt!

42
00:02:48,308 --> 00:02:50,613
This is driving me crazy.

43
00:02:50,807 --> 00:02:52,542
What are you talking about Gyu Rim now?

44
00:02:52,736 --> 00:02:54,638
Why would Gyu Rim get hurt?

45
00:02:54,838 --> 00:02:55,839
You two...

46
00:02:55,993 --> 00:03:00,252
Are you two just making things up
to give this old woman a heart attack?

47
00:03:00,277 --> 00:03:02,713
- Heung Sik, please. Move!
- Wait!

48
00:03:04,227 --> 00:03:07,326
Mom, I'll explain everything later,

49
00:03:07,785 --> 00:03:10,483
so for now, keep a tight hold on her
so she can't go anywhere.

50
00:03:10,754 --> 00:03:13,590
Her husband is a total lunatic,

51
00:03:13,616 --> 00:03:16,688
and Gyu Rim's with that lunatic right now,
so I have to hurry.

52
00:03:16,867 --> 00:03:18,432
I'm the one who has to go.

53
00:03:18,595 --> 00:03:21,369
I'm the one he wants to see!

54
00:03:21,799 --> 00:03:23,584
Go on, Heung Sik! Hurry!

55
00:03:23,667 --> 00:03:24,890
Su Nam!

56
00:03:24,915 --> 00:03:29,129
Gyu Rim's in danger!
What are you waiting for? Go!

57
00:03:29,212 --> 00:03:31,114
You said it's in front of Exit 5
of the subway station, right?

58
00:03:32,509 --> 00:03:33,777
Heung Sik!

59
00:03:33,857 --> 00:03:37,951
I'm going to break your legs.

60
00:03:37,995 --> 00:03:42,085
Once I take care of this,
you're going to pay,

61
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:43,780
so don't you move an inch.

62
00:03:44,013 --> 00:03:46,002
You conniving little bitch!

63
00:03:46,216 --> 00:03:48,692
You sneaky, shameless witch!

64
00:03:48,993 --> 00:03:51,716
Su Nam!

65
00:03:55,505 --> 00:03:57,141
Heung Sik!

66
00:03:59,115 --> 00:04:00,373
Gyu Rim!

67
00:04:06,703 --> 00:04:08,944
- Hello.
- Did you find Gyu Rim?

68
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:10,441
No.

69
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,743
I searched every cafe, restaurant, and bar
she might be at, but she's not there.

70
00:04:14,084 --> 00:04:15,486
Should I help look?

71
00:04:15,759 --> 00:04:18,224
No. It's fine. I'm hanging up.

72
00:04:20,484 --> 00:04:21,638
Gyu Rim!

73
00:04:22,859 --> 00:04:24,188
What is it with this woman...

74
00:04:30,614 --> 00:04:32,219
If you keep mouthing off,

75
00:04:32,729 --> 00:04:34,464
I'll beat you to a pulp this time.

76
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:38,418
I won't spare you again
just because you're Gyu Yeong's sister.

77
00:04:42,939 --> 00:04:44,240
No!

78
00:04:44,982 --> 00:04:46,442
You're not going!

79
00:04:46,863 --> 00:04:49,059
You're not going near Gyu Yeong!

80
00:04:49,285 --> 00:04:50,381
Hey, let go of me!

81
00:04:50,407 --> 00:04:52,609
Let go! I said, let go!

82
00:04:54,331 --> 00:04:55,628
You little...

83
00:04:57,594 --> 00:05:00,020
Help!

84
00:05:00,045 --> 00:05:02,592
- Hey, let go!
- Please call the police!

85
00:05:03,045 --> 00:05:04,460
- He's tried to kill me before!
- Let go!

86
00:05:04,485 --> 00:05:06,360
- Please call the police!
- Hey, you!

87
00:05:06,385 --> 00:05:07,434
Hey!

88
00:05:18,475 --> 00:05:21,967
I won't let go! I can't!

89
00:05:21,992 --> 00:05:23,560
Let go.

90
00:05:24,101 --> 00:05:26,004
You crazy woman.

91
00:05:28,258 --> 00:05:30,093
You want to die?

92
00:05:30,801 --> 00:05:32,002
Gyu Rim!

93
00:05:35,566 --> 00:05:37,344
You messed with the wrong person.

94
00:05:37,369 --> 00:05:39,839
Someone you should never have touched.

95
00:05:42,253 --> 00:05:44,720
- Mu Jin!
- You're dead today, jerk.

96
00:05:46,582 --> 00:05:48,751
Gyu Rim, are you okay?

97
00:05:49,792 --> 00:05:51,294
The police are coming.

98
00:05:52,155 --> 00:05:54,424
The police are coming,
so don't do anything stupid.

99
00:06:12,836 --> 00:06:15,405
Let go!

100
00:06:17,274 --> 00:06:20,216
That'll leave a scar. Does it hurt a lot?

101
00:06:20,830 --> 00:06:22,946
It's fine. It won't scar.
It doesn't hurt at all.

102
00:06:22,971 --> 00:06:25,412
Look at you.
How can you say it doesn't hurt?

103
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:28,660
Detective, can't you just question me?

104
00:06:28,685 --> 00:06:30,220
Please send her to the hospital first,

105
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:31,688
- so she can get treated...
- Mu Jin!

106
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:35,983
He didn't do anything wrong, Detective.

107
00:06:36,008 --> 00:06:38,476
He did it for me.
He was trying to help me.

108
00:06:38,909 --> 00:06:40,103
Please consider the circumstances.

109
00:06:40,128 --> 00:06:42,107
No,
I don't need any special consideration.

110
00:06:42,132 --> 00:06:44,501
I'll take responsibility for what I did,

111
00:06:44,501 --> 00:06:47,576
so send Gyu Rim to the hospital first
and check for any other injuries.

112
00:06:47,601 --> 00:06:50,136
Get her an X-ray, a CT scan,

113
00:06:50,173 --> 00:06:51,175
- an MRI...
- Mu Jin!

114
00:06:51,374 --> 00:06:53,122
Enough! Okay?

115
00:06:53,537 --> 00:06:55,303
Excuse me, Mr. Kim Mu Jin.

116
00:06:55,425 --> 00:06:59,257
This isn't child's play, you two.

117
00:06:59,342 --> 00:07:02,828
You do know that Kang Seong Uk,
the man you attacked,

118
00:07:02,919 --> 00:07:06,096
lost consciousness and was rushed
to the hospital, right?

119
00:07:06,396 --> 00:07:08,886
He's just pretending to be unconscious!

120
00:07:08,911 --> 00:07:11,896
If Gyu Rim hadn't stopped me,
I would've killed him today!

121
00:07:12,175 --> 00:07:13,927
Mu Jin, please. Okay?

122
00:07:14,376 --> 00:07:16,108
You can't just say whatever you want
because you're angry!

123
00:07:16,133 --> 00:07:17,843
This is a police station!

124
00:07:17,868 --> 00:07:20,522
- Chef!
- Yeah.

125
00:07:21,658 --> 00:07:25,439
I got some ointment, disinfectant,
and first aid supplies for now.

126
00:07:27,570 --> 00:07:31,135
I'll take care of the wounds myself,
so let's focus on the questioning.

127
00:07:31,828 --> 00:07:35,026
- I'm serious. I'll get mad.
- Okay.

128
00:07:35,258 --> 00:07:36,760
I mean it.

129
00:07:37,354 --> 00:07:40,950
I've questioned suspects for ten years,
but I've never seen one like this.

130
00:07:41,337 --> 00:07:42,820
- Mr. Kim Mu Jin.
- Yes.

131
00:07:43,026 --> 00:07:48,349
You're at a police station,
being questioned as a suspect.

132
00:07:48,625 --> 00:07:53,879
This could be obstruction of justice
and hurt your case, Mr. Kim.

133
00:07:54,790 --> 00:07:57,759
I'm really sorry.

134
00:07:58,542 --> 00:08:02,246
So you'd never met the victim,
Mr. Kang Seong Uk, before?

135
00:08:02,713 --> 00:08:03,867
And,

136
00:08:04,054 --> 00:08:08,204
instead of asking what happened,

137
00:08:08,251 --> 00:08:11,566
you just launched into a flying kick.
Right?

138
00:08:12,022 --> 00:08:14,725
That jerk deserved it.

139
00:08:14,784 --> 00:08:19,773
If I'd found him first,
I'd have beaten him to death myself.

140
00:08:19,889 --> 00:08:21,934
- And who might you be?
- Me?

141
00:08:23,875 --> 00:08:26,845
I know these two very well,

142
00:08:26,870 --> 00:08:28,972
and that jerk Kang Seong Uk...

143
00:08:32,348 --> 00:08:34,256
I know him well too.

144
00:08:34,363 --> 00:08:37,366
I witnessed the whole thing myself.

145
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:41,481
If you're a witness,
please wait until I ask you something.

146
00:08:42,385 --> 00:08:43,886
Yes.

147
00:08:44,588 --> 00:08:48,594
Mr. Kim hit him so hard,
you know, Mr. Kang Seong Uk's teeth?

148
00:08:48,792 --> 00:08:51,261
He lost eight of them. Eight!

149
00:08:51,628 --> 00:08:55,632
With violence this severe,
I doubt you'll reach a settlement.

150
00:08:56,333 --> 00:08:59,611
- I won't settle with a jerk like him.
- No, that's not it.

151
00:08:59,636 --> 00:09:04,028
I pulled six of his teeth myself.

152
00:09:04,441 --> 00:09:09,521
They're not real teeth anyway, so whether
he eats taffy or tears into squid...

153
00:09:09,546 --> 00:09:12,616
Witness, when I ask you a question,

154
00:09:12,795 --> 00:09:16,565
that's when you answer.

155
00:09:17,854 --> 00:09:19,748
Yes, okay.

156
00:09:21,144 --> 00:09:24,314
Detective, please consider that.

157
00:09:24,762 --> 00:09:28,565
Kang Seong Uk is a dangerous man
who can't be reasoned with,

158
00:09:28,845 --> 00:09:30,438
and he's an attempted murderer.

159
00:09:30,901 --> 00:09:34,204
Not long ago, he even deliberately
tried to run me over.

160
00:09:34,229 --> 00:09:36,871
What do you mean?
He tried to run you over?

161
00:09:37,359 --> 00:09:38,695
Is that true?

162
00:09:38,809 --> 00:09:41,253
Which hospital is that jerk in?

163
00:09:41,278 --> 00:09:43,146
I need to kill him right now.

164
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:44,558
Mu Jin, calm down!

165
00:09:44,915 --> 00:09:46,516
I didn't tell you this
to get you worked up.

166
00:09:46,541 --> 00:09:48,889
Stay out of it. I'll handle it myself.

167
00:09:48,958 --> 00:09:50,896
Please don't do this.

168
00:09:51,288 --> 00:09:53,238
This isn't helping me, Mu Jin.

169
00:09:53,423 --> 00:09:55,901
Why do you keep making me look
like I'm a burden to everyone?

170
00:09:55,926 --> 00:09:57,922
That jerk tried to run you over.

171
00:09:57,947 --> 00:09:59,282
You could've died!

172
00:09:59,329 --> 00:10:01,907
But I didn't! I'm right here, alive!

173
00:10:01,932 --> 00:10:04,063
You still got hurt!

174
00:10:07,256 --> 00:10:10,927
It hurts me more when
you get hurt, Mu Jin.

175
00:10:11,942 --> 00:10:14,244
It hurts me even more
when you're the one who's hurt, Mu Jin.

176
00:10:14,244 --> 00:10:17,447
If anything happened to you because of me,
that would be worse than any violence.

177
00:10:18,695 --> 00:10:20,497
So please, don't do this.

178
00:10:21,852 --> 00:10:24,955
I'm already having a hard enough time
as it is, Mu Jin.

179
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:26,777
So please.

180
00:10:27,477 --> 00:10:30,220
I'm begging you. Please don't do this.

181
00:10:38,908 --> 00:10:42,590
Hello. I'm Mr. Kim Mu Jin's lawyer.

182
00:10:51,929 --> 00:10:53,764
It's okay.

183
00:10:54,885 --> 00:10:58,688
Seong Uk got beaten up by Kim Mu Jin
and was taken to the hospital,

184
00:10:58,755 --> 00:11:01,057
and Gyu Rim is perfectly fine,
so don't worry!

185
00:11:03,093 --> 00:11:06,563
That's all. I'm hanging up now.

186
00:11:13,623 --> 00:11:17,193
What did Heung Sik say? How's Gyu Rim?

187
00:11:19,309 --> 00:11:22,495
She's okay. He says she's safe.

188
00:11:24,987 --> 00:11:28,062
Thank goodness.

189
00:11:37,894 --> 00:11:41,031
Now that Gyu Rim's okay,

190
00:11:42,058 --> 00:11:44,961
come here.

191
00:11:45,309 --> 00:11:49,146
You're as good as dead now.

192
00:11:49,171 --> 00:11:52,308
Come on. Right in front of me.

193
00:12:04,775 --> 00:12:06,551
You think a flyswatter will do the job?

194
00:12:07,410 --> 00:12:08,778
What?

195
00:12:08,945 --> 00:12:15,129
I'm not a fly. You could swat me all day,
and I still wouldn't die.

196
00:12:16,245 --> 00:12:18,430
Don't you have a hammer
or a saw or something?

197
00:12:19,622 --> 00:12:23,646
A hammer or a saw?

198
00:12:24,307 --> 00:12:26,685
Are you challenging me now?

199
00:12:27,857 --> 00:12:33,312
Who are you to tell me
what I should use to kill you?

200
00:12:33,850 --> 00:12:36,486
I'll just keep hitting you with this
until you die.

201
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:39,644
Have you ever been swatted to death
with a flyswatter?

202
00:12:39,788 --> 00:12:44,260
If you're going to kill me,
just do it in one shot.

203
00:12:45,274 --> 00:12:51,347
I have nothing left to live for,
and I don't even want to live anymore.

204
00:12:51,372 --> 00:12:54,421
Are you threatening an old woman?

205
00:12:55,486 --> 00:13:01,444
You're the one at fault,
and you have the nerve to get angry?

206
00:13:01,884 --> 00:13:06,122
Fine, even this flyswatter
is too good for you.

207
00:13:07,690 --> 00:13:11,127
I'll get a needle and keep poking you,
for months, even years,

208
00:13:11,221 --> 00:13:17,230
until you die in agony.

209
00:13:17,506 --> 00:13:20,301
Just kill me in one go.

210
00:13:21,357 --> 00:13:26,271
I'm Han Gyu Rim's sister,
the girl you adore so much.

211
00:13:26,868 --> 00:13:30,863
You can at least show me that much mercy.

212
00:13:33,449 --> 00:13:37,588
I won't object,
so go ahead and get your revenge.

213
00:13:37,861 --> 00:13:39,704
No hard feelings. Just make it quick.

214
00:13:41,651 --> 00:13:47,337
What a nasty piece of work.

215
00:14:03,204 --> 00:14:05,001
Fine. Then we'll both die today.

216
00:14:05,026 --> 00:14:07,695
I'll beat you to a pulp.

217
00:14:07,977 --> 00:14:09,403
And I'll get the needle.

218
00:14:30,338 --> 00:14:32,482
They let him go?

219
00:14:33,015 --> 00:14:37,848
He's identified and not a flight risk,
so he's been released for now.

220
00:14:38,367 --> 00:14:41,383
- Where's Gyu Rim?
- She went to the restroom.

221
00:14:41,845 --> 00:14:46,909
She's putting on ointment and fixing up
her hair so her family won't worry.

222
00:14:47,837 --> 00:14:51,468
Did you hear which hospital
that jerk Kang Seong Uk was taken to?

223
00:14:51,493 --> 00:14:54,461
Why? So you can go there
and kill him yourself?

224
00:14:54,486 --> 00:14:55,563
Yeah.

225
00:14:55,992 --> 00:15:00,339
If you kill him and go to jail,
do you think Gyu Rim will be okay?

226
00:15:00,543 --> 00:15:03,174
You want to see her lose her mind,
you idiot?

227
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:08,652
This cricket isn't wrong
about a single thing,

228
00:15:09,959 --> 00:15:16,081
but I was really impressed
by how bold you were, Mr. Kim.

229
00:15:17,112 --> 00:15:20,301
You're exactly my type.

230
00:15:20,423 --> 00:15:23,550
I'm a huge fan now.

231
00:15:24,053 --> 00:15:25,753
Fan, my foot.

232
00:15:25,789 --> 00:15:27,779
Hey, Mr. Monkey.

233
00:15:29,552 --> 00:15:30,953
Mu Jin.

234
00:15:31,481 --> 00:15:33,559
Let's stop being so formal,

235
00:15:33,963 --> 00:15:37,541
and just talk like friends from now on.
You too, Cricket.

236
00:15:38,955 --> 00:15:40,990
I've got plenty of friends
back in Wando already.

237
00:15:43,239 --> 00:15:45,608
We'll have to talk that over first.

238
00:15:46,415 --> 00:15:48,083
But what's taking Gyu Rim so long?

239
00:15:48,217 --> 00:15:49,552
Shouldn't we go check on her?

240
00:15:50,265 --> 00:15:51,597
What's taking her so long?

241
00:15:51,622 --> 00:15:52,990
Here she comes!

242
00:15:54,417 --> 00:15:55,618
Gyu Rim.

243
00:16:00,436 --> 00:16:03,193
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine. Are you okay?

244
00:16:03,218 --> 00:16:04,953
No, let's get you to the hospital first.

245
00:16:05,455 --> 00:16:08,107
I'm really fine.
It's not bad enough to go to the hospital.

246
00:16:08,132 --> 00:16:11,021
No. You could have a head injury,

247
00:16:11,046 --> 00:16:13,603
or internal injuries we can't see.

248
00:16:13,628 --> 00:16:16,667
- I need to go see Gyu Yeong.
- Why?

249
00:16:19,214 --> 00:16:22,976
If I feel even a little off,
I'll go to the hospital. Okay?

250
00:16:27,483 --> 00:16:29,502
I can't exactly praise you, Mu Jin,

251
00:16:29,739 --> 00:16:32,356
for what you did today.

252
00:16:35,118 --> 00:16:36,619
But I'm still grateful. Thank you.

253
00:16:39,408 --> 00:16:41,098
Thank you for saving me.

254
00:16:43,346 --> 00:16:45,957
But this is where it ends.

255
00:16:46,749 --> 00:16:49,645
Please, let it end here.

256
00:16:51,747 --> 00:16:52,848
Okay.

257
00:16:53,837 --> 00:16:55,092
I'm leaving.

258
00:17:05,061 --> 00:17:09,010
- Please don't get hurt.
- I won't.

259
00:17:09,365 --> 00:17:10,881
- I'm leaving.
- Okay.

260
00:17:12,562 --> 00:17:15,732
All right. See you later.

261
00:17:16,178 --> 00:17:19,045
Cricket, you worked really hard too.

262
00:17:19,636 --> 00:17:21,891
I'm off. Gyu Rim, come with me!

263
00:17:22,905 --> 00:17:25,750
I want to live like a cricket...

264
00:17:25,775 --> 00:17:30,146
in peace with beetles and other bugs.
I really do.

265
00:17:31,114 --> 00:17:35,960
I don't want to be around primates,
like monkeys or humans. No way.

266
00:17:35,985 --> 00:17:39,222
Why is her whole family like that?

267
00:17:39,656 --> 00:17:42,401
Fix one thing, and another blows up.
Fix that, and something else blows up.

268
00:17:42,521 --> 00:17:43,861
What is this, whack-a-mole?

269
00:17:44,460 --> 00:17:47,163
Can't they leave Gyu Rim alone
for one day so she can breathe?

270
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:49,704
I'm so afraid she'll just blow away
that I can barely breathe myself,

271
00:17:50,266 --> 00:17:52,568
so why does everyone keep hurting her
when she's as fragile as a leaf?

272
00:17:52,602 --> 00:17:53,970
Those damn jerks.

273
00:17:54,971 --> 00:17:57,407
Hey, should I just adopt Gyu Rim?

274
00:17:57,726 --> 00:17:59,725
- Did you like it?
- Like what?

275
00:18:03,992 --> 00:18:05,594
I didn't expect that either.

276
00:18:18,279 --> 00:18:19,669
Gyu Yeong!

277
00:18:22,411 --> 00:18:24,158
What are you doing here?

278
00:18:27,577 --> 00:18:29,243
Did my mom kick you out?

279
00:18:36,239 --> 00:18:38,074
This is for food and lodging.

280
00:18:38,293 --> 00:18:39,928
If it's not enough,
I'll give you more later.

281
00:18:40,416 --> 00:18:41,619
Put that away.

282
00:18:41,684 --> 00:18:43,606
Food and lodging? Between us?

283
00:18:44,901 --> 00:18:46,769
You got kicked out too.

284
00:18:47,089 --> 00:18:51,177
Your mom changed all the door codes
and told you never to come back.

285
00:18:58,921 --> 00:19:00,089
Where are you going?

286
00:19:00,603 --> 00:19:03,164
Don't look down on me
just because I've hit rock bottom.

287
00:19:03,239 --> 00:19:04,874
Don't act like we're close.

288
00:19:09,366 --> 00:19:10,533
Let go.

289
00:19:13,062 --> 00:19:16,874
Hey, let go! Let go of me!

290
00:19:17,766 --> 00:19:19,335
Let's go home, Gyu Yeong.

291
00:19:20,056 --> 00:19:21,557
Come home with me.

292
00:19:21,791 --> 00:19:24,127
No. Why would I go there?

293
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:28,281
Even if I have to walk into a lion's den,
I'm never going back to that house.

294
00:19:28,511 --> 00:19:29,645
Let go!

295
00:19:32,935 --> 00:19:35,779
I'll hold her. You let go.

296
00:19:36,105 --> 00:19:38,709
You're so worn out,
you can barely breathe.

297
00:19:38,841 --> 00:19:40,242
Heung Sik!

298
00:19:41,978 --> 00:19:44,414
I knew you'd be stubborn,
so I called Gyu O.

299
00:19:44,714 --> 00:19:46,282
- He'll be here soon.
- Hey.

300
00:19:46,382 --> 00:19:50,227
You're completely surrounded,
so stay put and surrender.

301
00:19:50,686 --> 00:19:54,265
Who do you think you are?

302
00:19:54,290 --> 00:19:57,969
Where I go is none of your business.
Why are you restricting my freedom?

303
00:19:58,094 --> 00:20:00,129
Why can't you mind your own business?

304
00:20:00,268 --> 00:20:01,737
Let go of me!

305
00:20:02,257 --> 00:20:03,701
For crying out loud!

306
00:20:11,407 --> 00:20:13,776
Yeah. I knew something was off.

307
00:20:14,096 --> 00:20:16,736
I had a feeling something was up
when we met at the cold noodle place.

308
00:20:17,513 --> 00:20:19,215
Shut your mouth.

309
00:20:20,216 --> 00:20:22,816
How far have you spread the word?
What exactly did you tell them?

310
00:20:22,919 --> 00:20:25,755
Did you tell Dad and Gyeol that
Gyu Yeong, who acted so high and mighty,

311
00:20:25,948 --> 00:20:29,383
fell victim to marriage fraud
and had her life ruined?

312
00:20:29,718 --> 00:20:34,020
Why not grab a megaphone and tell
the whole neighborhood? All of Korea?

313
00:20:34,223 --> 00:20:35,321
Should I?

314
00:20:35,598 --> 00:20:38,176
Gyu O, want to go get a megaphone?

315
00:20:38,201 --> 00:20:39,602
Hey, Han Gyu Rim!

316
00:20:43,239 --> 00:20:45,671
- Hey, that's mine!
- What now?

317
00:20:45,908 --> 00:20:48,377
- Want me to load you in like luggage too?
- What?

318
00:20:48,652 --> 00:20:50,847
Just say the word.

319
00:20:51,006 --> 00:20:53,900
I can haul a kid around like luggage.
It's no trouble at all.

320
00:20:55,084 --> 00:20:56,537
Just get in.

321
00:20:56,562 --> 00:20:58,843
Heung Sik, I said I'm not going.

322
00:20:59,167 --> 00:21:00,890
- Just get in already!
- Seriously.

323
00:21:03,693 --> 00:21:06,203
Hey, get in the front.
Am I your chauffeur?

324
00:21:06,228 --> 00:21:07,629
Shut up!

325
00:21:13,195 --> 00:21:14,463
You okay?

326
00:21:16,892 --> 00:21:18,460
Thank you, Heung Sik.

327
00:21:19,221 --> 00:21:23,258
Gyu Yeong must've been terrified
with nowhere else to go,

328
00:21:23,779 --> 00:21:26,349
so I'm really grateful
you were there to protect her.

329
00:21:26,622 --> 00:21:29,258
You would've done the same, wouldn't you?

330
00:21:31,620 --> 00:21:34,879
I'll get going, Heung Sik.
I'll call you. Thank you.

331
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:42,055
Wait, Gyu Rim.

332
00:21:49,322 --> 00:21:51,098
Can't you take me with you too?

333
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:55,180
My mom probably won't even open
the door for me right now,

334
00:21:56,050 --> 00:21:59,854
and if she catches me,
I'm as good as dead.

335
00:22:07,343 --> 00:22:09,352
So that woman...

336
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:13,018
That stalker lady is our mom...

337
00:22:23,567 --> 00:22:25,814
How long has she been following us?

338
00:22:26,654 --> 00:22:28,824
She seems to know everything about us,

339
00:22:30,478 --> 00:22:34,411
and since she even went to see
Gyu Rim's mom, she knows our address too.

340
00:22:35,027 --> 00:22:37,225
It's only a matter of time
before she shows up at our house.

341
00:22:40,808 --> 00:22:43,886
Do you maybe have a thing for Seok Jung?

342
00:22:43,911 --> 00:22:45,709
You little brat!

343
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:49,813
I said, let go of me!

344
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:55,065
It's much worse than I thought,

345
00:22:56,364 --> 00:22:59,448
even more pathetic and horrible
than I ever imagined.

346
00:23:02,739 --> 00:23:03,968
What?

347
00:23:05,327 --> 00:23:07,488
Too shocked to even speak?

348
00:23:15,774 --> 00:23:18,402
What if that woman says
she's moving back into our house?

349
00:23:22,047 --> 00:23:23,989
I'm asking you, Han Gyu Seo!
What are we going to do?

350
00:23:24,389 --> 00:23:25,762
Just let her try.

351
00:23:27,071 --> 00:23:28,661
You think I'll let her get away with this?

352
00:23:32,651 --> 00:23:35,126
I'm already stressed enough about Gyu O.

353
00:23:40,059 --> 00:23:43,801
Let's keep this between us for now.

354
00:23:46,664 --> 00:23:48,034
Let's keep it a secret.

355
00:24:02,083 --> 00:24:03,207
I prayed...

356
00:24:04,731 --> 00:24:07,970
that if Gyu O got better and was forgiven,

357
00:24:08,913 --> 00:24:10,251
then out of Dad, Han Gyu Yeong, Mom...

358
00:24:12,336 --> 00:24:13,566
I mean,

359
00:24:16,231 --> 00:24:19,822
that woman,
I promised I'd forgive one of them.

360
00:24:21,667 --> 00:24:23,292
That woman doesn't count, though.

361
00:24:26,620 --> 00:24:29,928
So, between Dad and Han Gyu Yeong,
who do you think is better?

362
00:24:39,980 --> 00:24:43,501
Come on, just once. Please?

363
00:24:43,526 --> 00:24:45,912
I said no! Not once, not twice!

364
00:24:47,894 --> 00:24:49,299
Why not?

365
00:24:49,660 --> 00:24:53,356
It's not like I'm asking you
to take me to some rebel hideout.

366
00:24:53,381 --> 00:24:55,011
I'm just asking for your teacher's number.

367
00:24:55,047 --> 00:24:58,508
Just eight of the 11 digits.
Why can't you tell me?

368
00:24:58,573 --> 00:25:01,836
Those eight digits don't even include
the 010 prefix.

369
00:25:02,347 --> 00:25:05,414
Fine, include the 010.
Just give me all 11 digits.

370
00:25:05,729 --> 00:25:09,221
No! How can I give out
someone else's personal information?

371
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:11,825
Hey, your teacher isn't a stranger.

372
00:25:12,134 --> 00:25:13,218
She's going to be part of our family...

373
00:25:13,607 --> 00:25:15,583
I mean, your future aunt...

374
00:25:17,187 --> 00:25:21,439
Anyway, I really need to meet
your teacher and talk to her.

375
00:25:21,723 --> 00:25:24,834
What do you need to tell my teacher,
Grandpa?

376
00:25:24,859 --> 00:25:26,426
Tell me first.

377
00:25:27,540 --> 00:25:31,019
How can a kid be this hard to persuade?

378
00:25:33,207 --> 00:25:34,228
What's that?

379
00:25:35,582 --> 00:25:36,753
What's going on?

380
00:25:37,605 --> 00:25:40,271
Hello, Mr. Han. Hi, Gyeol.

381
00:25:40,671 --> 00:25:42,065
Hello.

382
00:25:42,672 --> 00:25:43,804
What brings you here?

383
00:25:44,266 --> 00:25:46,180
What's this? Is this yours?

384
00:25:47,514 --> 00:25:48,554
It's not that.

385
00:25:48,579 --> 00:25:51,820
Han Gyu Yeong is coming in.
Don't react or show any interest.

386
00:25:52,061 --> 00:25:54,784
Don't ask why she's here.
Don't ask her anything.

387
00:25:54,853 --> 00:25:56,279
Just pretend she's invisible.

388
00:25:57,137 --> 00:25:58,855
What are you talking about?

389
00:25:59,347 --> 00:26:03,567
Why is Gyu Yeong coming so late?
And what's this about ignoring her?

390
00:26:03,632 --> 00:26:08,044
I'll explain everything later.
Just leave Gyu Yeong alone tonight.

391
00:26:08,947 --> 00:26:10,651
Gyeol, when you see Gyu Yeong,

392
00:26:14,078 --> 00:26:15,501
just pretend she's invisible too.

393
00:26:15,693 --> 00:26:17,807
Not even saying hello to an adult?

394
00:26:18,614 --> 00:26:22,326
No, wait, you should greet adults.
With a smile, okay?

395
00:26:22,526 --> 00:26:24,192
But I'm not happy to see her.

396
00:26:25,864 --> 00:26:28,804
This is all so sudden,

397
00:26:29,019 --> 00:26:30,934
and I can't make sense of any of it.

398
00:26:31,320 --> 00:26:32,899
Do you understand what he's saying?

399
00:26:33,220 --> 00:26:36,081
Yes. Not everything, but most of it.

400
00:26:36,327 --> 00:26:38,403
You might be the ticking time bomb,
Mr. Han.

401
00:26:38,895 --> 00:26:40,146
Wait a moment.

402
00:26:40,252 --> 00:26:42,521
Put this on first. It's brand new.

403
00:26:42,546 --> 00:26:45,102
What are you doing?

404
00:26:47,170 --> 00:26:49,468
It might feel uncomfortable,
but just bear with it, okay?

405
00:26:49,493 --> 00:26:51,666
Isn't this better than having her run off?

406
00:26:53,474 --> 00:26:55,023
Dad, why don't you stay in your room?

407
00:26:55,444 --> 00:26:58,834
- Let go. I said I'm not going in.
- Come on, hurry up.

408
00:26:58,859 --> 00:27:00,365
- I'm not going in there.
- Gyu O.

409
00:27:00,412 --> 00:27:02,756
- Yeah.
- Hey, I said I'm not going in.

410
00:27:02,784 --> 00:27:04,246
I said I'm not going in!

411
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:11,834
Your foot.

412
00:27:13,312 --> 00:27:14,668
- Hey.
- Right foot.

413
00:27:14,814 --> 00:27:16,579
Seriously!

414
00:27:19,179 --> 00:27:22,672
- Good evening, Gyu Yeong.
- Nothing good about it.

415
00:27:23,460 --> 00:27:26,499
Dad, I brought Gyu Yeong home.

416
00:27:27,074 --> 00:27:30,010
I didn't think she should live
cut off from us like that,

417
00:27:30,493 --> 00:27:33,558
and I figured she'd be better off
with us than those people,

418
00:27:33,682 --> 00:27:35,295
so I just brought her back by force.

419
00:28:01,694 --> 00:28:05,391
Tell her she's been through a lot
and that you're glad she's home.

420
00:28:06,737 --> 00:28:08,686
Give her a warm welcome.

421
00:28:12,701 --> 00:28:14,326
You did well holding back.

422
00:28:18,884 --> 00:28:20,008
Mr. Han.

423
00:28:35,779 --> 00:28:38,270
Mom, what happened to your face?

424
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:41,674
- What about my face?
- Bandages.

425
00:28:42,507 --> 00:28:44,291
Did you get into a fight?

426
00:28:45,061 --> 00:28:47,510
This? Well...

427
00:28:48,879 --> 00:28:52,566
Did you get hurt fighting
to bring Gyu Yeong home?

428
00:28:53,799 --> 00:28:54,906
Yeah.

429
00:28:55,834 --> 00:28:59,968
Even grown-ups sometimes fight
to protect something that matters.

430
00:29:01,493 --> 00:29:03,016
But I won.

431
00:29:04,058 --> 00:29:05,081
Mom.

432
00:29:39,523 --> 00:29:41,047
Gyu Yeong...

433
00:29:42,664 --> 00:29:45,194
She got caught committing fraud
and got kicked out, didn't she?

434
00:29:45,876 --> 00:29:49,327
She wasn't kicked out.
She left on her own.

435
00:29:49,590 --> 00:29:54,360
Kicked out or walked out,
she still got caught committing fraud.

436
00:29:54,722 --> 00:29:58,639
Being kicked out and walking out
are completely different things.

437
00:30:02,126 --> 00:30:06,960
I always had a bad feeling about her.

438
00:30:14,943 --> 00:30:18,167
Gyu Yeong went down
the wrong path for a while,

439
00:30:18,809 --> 00:30:21,991
but she realized she'd made a mistake
and chose to get back on the right path.

440
00:30:22,730 --> 00:30:24,503
So please don't cry, Dad.

441
00:30:53,307 --> 00:30:54,595
Aren't you leaving?

442
00:31:00,014 --> 00:31:01,841
Quite a show, isn't it?

443
00:31:02,079 --> 00:31:04,949
You wished this awful brat
would crash and burn,

444
00:31:05,279 --> 00:31:09,232
and now you've got a front-row seat
to my life falling apart. Must be a blast.

445
00:31:15,758 --> 00:31:20,531
I'll send you an ultra-HD video
of what a wreck I am,

446
00:31:21,212 --> 00:31:24,305
so if you ever need a laugh,
just play it on repeat. Now get out!

447
00:31:24,358 --> 00:31:27,739
Get out! Stop staring and leave!

448
00:31:31,953 --> 00:31:33,689
Why would I go out of my way to watch?

449
00:31:34,280 --> 00:31:37,761
If I want to see someone hit rock bottom,
I only have to look in the mirror.

450
00:31:38,513 --> 00:31:39,840
What are you talking about?

451
00:31:41,754 --> 00:31:44,648
Is it payback season these days?

452
00:31:45,032 --> 00:31:47,134
Or harvest season,
when you reap what you sow?

453
00:31:48,818 --> 00:31:51,746
You plant soybeans, you get soybeans.
You plant red beans, you get red beans.

454
00:31:52,837 --> 00:31:54,854
Nature's laws are pretty scary, right?

455
00:31:55,150 --> 00:31:56,590
I said, what are you talking about?

456
00:31:58,994 --> 00:32:00,385
Have you hit rock bottom already?

457
00:32:00,695 --> 00:32:02,401
Why? What happened?

458
00:32:03,181 --> 00:32:06,221
Su Nam told me you'd become
a clothing store owner. Isn't that right?

459
00:32:08,285 --> 00:32:10,176
I'd planted some red beans before,

460
00:32:10,803 --> 00:32:13,977
and I thought if I played my cards right,
maybe soybeans would sprout instead,

461
00:32:14,551 --> 00:32:16,199
but sure enough, red beans came up.

462
00:32:18,719 --> 00:32:21,002
A middle-school grad using metaphors
on someone with a PhD?

463
00:32:21,194 --> 00:32:23,243
Have you been hanging out
with someone smart lately?

464
00:32:31,514 --> 00:32:32,731
What is this now?

465
00:32:33,287 --> 00:32:36,041
I hit rock bottom too,
but I climbed back up today.

466
00:32:36,880 --> 00:32:40,593
Thanks to Gyu Rim, Gyu Seo, and Gyu Min.
Thanks to our family.

467
00:32:41,393 --> 00:32:43,868
Gyu Rim and the twins
reached out and took my hand.

468
00:32:46,214 --> 00:32:49,625
I'll take your hand too.
So grab it and climb back up.

469
00:32:53,376 --> 00:32:54,605
No, thanks.

470
00:32:55,190 --> 00:32:58,358
Go play your games among yourselves,
for all I care!

471
00:33:00,067 --> 00:33:02,185
Don't you dare interfere in my life.

472
00:33:02,533 --> 00:33:05,640
I'm not like you. Even at my worst,
I'm still Han Gyu Yeong. Got it?

473
00:33:06,864 --> 00:33:09,121
Han Gyu Yeong is here? Upstairs?

474
00:33:09,385 --> 00:33:12,219
Yeah. Mom brought Gyu Yeong home.

475
00:33:12,626 --> 00:33:14,163
No way.

476
00:33:20,567 --> 00:33:22,199
My mom got hurt.

477
00:33:22,487 --> 00:33:24,718
She got into a fight to bring her home.

478
00:33:24,946 --> 00:33:26,449
Really?

479
00:33:26,917 --> 00:33:28,631
Just act like you don't know.

480
00:33:30,074 --> 00:33:32,793
Tell her you're glad she's home
and that she's been through a lot.

481
00:33:32,843 --> 00:33:34,834
Give her a warm welcome.
That's what Mom said.

482
00:33:38,265 --> 00:33:40,367
The good days are over now.

483
00:34:30,917 --> 00:34:32,172
Are you crying?

484
00:34:37,047 --> 00:34:40,704
I want to cry, but I can't.

485
00:34:42,617 --> 00:34:44,944
Old sayings are always right.

486
00:34:44,969 --> 00:34:46,809
Stay close to a bad person,
and you'll get struck by lightning too.

487
00:34:48,703 --> 00:34:51,331
That's what someone said
in a drama earlier.

488
00:34:52,186 --> 00:34:53,810
Is that writer out of their mind?

489
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:55,906
So no one should ever associate
with someone who's done wrong?

490
00:34:56,414 --> 00:34:59,414
The world's cold enough as it is,
and now a drama is encouraging bullying?

491
00:34:59,439 --> 00:35:01,719
I'm leaving that writer a nasty comment.

492
00:35:04,549 --> 00:35:08,088
You're really not going to settle
with Kang Seong Uk?

493
00:35:08,165 --> 00:35:09,348
No.

494
00:35:09,465 --> 00:35:12,546
Put your feelings aside
and think logically.

495
00:35:12,980 --> 00:35:15,289
Whatever the circumstances,

496
00:35:15,729 --> 00:35:18,634
you committed a serious act of violence
in a country governed by the rule of law.

497
00:35:18,659 --> 00:35:21,556
If you're punished for it,
how do you think Gyu Rim will feel?

498
00:35:21,806 --> 00:35:23,221
Aren't you thinking about her?

499
00:35:27,681 --> 00:35:30,938
How am I more worried about Gyu Rim
than you are?

500
00:35:32,076 --> 00:35:33,137
What's going on?

501
00:35:33,294 --> 00:35:36,077
I came in here fully intending
to badmouth Gyu Rim.

502
00:35:37,956 --> 00:35:39,059
Now I'm confused.

503
00:36:02,934 --> 00:36:03,980
Hello?

504
00:36:04,697 --> 00:36:06,536
Is this Kim Mu Jin?

505
00:36:08,597 --> 00:36:11,788
Yes, it is. Who's this?

506
00:36:13,227 --> 00:36:16,335
My name is Lee Hyeon Beom.

507
00:36:16,544 --> 00:36:19,037
Sorry? Who was that?

508
00:36:20,925 --> 00:36:22,633
Lee Hyeon Beom...

509
00:36:24,013 --> 00:36:26,381
I'm sorry, I don't recognize that name.

510
00:36:28,425 --> 00:36:29,566
Hello?

511
00:36:30,526 --> 00:36:35,048
You know Han Gyeol, right?
Han Gyu Rim's son.

512
00:36:37,062 --> 00:36:38,811
Yes, I do.

513
00:36:39,674 --> 00:36:43,508
I believe I'm Gyeol's biological father.

514
00:36:45,966 --> 00:36:47,119
What?

515
00:37:09,905 --> 00:37:11,981
Gyeol, lift your head.

516
00:37:33,386 --> 00:37:34,884
It's okay.

517
00:37:35,940 --> 00:37:37,611
This will all pass.

518
00:37:39,198 --> 00:37:40,630
Right, Gyeol?

519
00:37:43,018 --> 00:37:44,651
It'll all pass.

520
00:37:47,094 --> 00:37:48,248
Right?

521
00:38:32,854 --> 00:38:34,659
(Seo Min Ju)

522
00:38:44,571 --> 00:38:46,918
You're actually answering?

523
00:38:53,150 --> 00:38:55,864
I thought you'd blocked my number,
but you picked up.

524
00:38:58,229 --> 00:39:01,973
Hello? Are you even listening?

525
00:39:03,736 --> 00:39:07,480
Hey, Kwon Hui Na! Are you listening to me?

526
00:39:10,405 --> 00:39:13,856
Hello?

527
00:39:15,367 --> 00:39:18,548
Hey, Kwon Hui Na. Can you hear me?

528
00:39:19,579 --> 00:39:20,640
Hey!

529
00:39:23,089 --> 00:39:24,577
Why isn't she answering?

530
00:39:39,098 --> 00:39:40,413
Don't go, Hui Na.

531
00:39:41,903 --> 00:39:43,604
Hui Na, don't go.

532
00:40:29,378 --> 00:40:31,804
- Gyu Rim.
- Yes?

533
00:40:45,370 --> 00:40:47,892
Dad asked you to make ramen
this early in the morning?

534
00:40:48,860 --> 00:40:50,714
Is Heung Sik coming to eat too?

535
00:40:52,093 --> 00:40:55,059
- Still, seven packs are way too much...
- No, they're mine.

536
00:40:55,574 --> 00:40:57,614
I suddenly got a huge craving for ramen.

537
00:40:59,387 --> 00:41:01,847
You're not eating all
of that yourself, are you?

538
00:41:02,373 --> 00:41:03,851
I am.

539
00:41:04,094 --> 00:41:06,974
It's all mine, so make your own
if you want some.

540
00:41:09,073 --> 00:41:10,642
I should add some rice too.

541
00:41:10,909 --> 00:41:12,631
There should be some leftover rice.

542
00:41:13,288 --> 00:41:16,162
- Gyu Min, you're up early.
- Yeah.

543
00:41:17,114 --> 00:41:19,202
Where was it?

544
00:41:21,830 --> 00:41:23,005
Here it is.

545
00:41:45,318 --> 00:41:46,548
Han Gyu Seo.

546
00:41:47,029 --> 00:41:48,258
Han Gyu Seo, wake up.

547
00:41:49,172 --> 00:41:50,400
I said wake up.

548
00:41:51,053 --> 00:41:53,556
I fell asleep at dawn.
Just five more minutes.

549
00:41:55,859 --> 00:41:57,745
I'm telling you, Gyu Rim made ramen.

550
00:41:57,827 --> 00:42:01,127
Seven packs at once,
and she's going to eat them all herself.

551
00:42:01,234 --> 00:42:03,257
Get up!

552
00:42:07,047 --> 00:42:08,245
Seven?

553
00:42:09,447 --> 00:42:12,057
Yeah. She's even adding rice today.

554
00:42:12,907 --> 00:42:14,218
She's adding rice too?

555
00:42:37,194 --> 00:42:38,268
Hey!

556
00:42:42,946 --> 00:42:44,756
Why are you eating my ramen?

557
00:42:44,995 --> 00:42:46,797
I told you to make your own.

558
00:42:47,609 --> 00:42:50,263
Ramen always tastes better
when someone else makes it.

559
00:42:54,024 --> 00:42:55,560
You're unbelievable.

560
00:43:08,646 --> 00:43:10,013
Han Gyu O!

561
00:43:12,587 --> 00:43:15,120
This is all mine. I'm eating it all.

562
00:43:17,540 --> 00:43:19,681
How are you going to finish all that?

563
00:43:19,754 --> 00:43:22,154
Have you lost your mind?
You want to eat until you burst?

564
00:43:22,327 --> 00:43:23,478
Exactly.

565
00:43:27,567 --> 00:43:30,091
Share at least one noodle. We're family.

566
00:43:30,834 --> 00:43:33,068
Hey, didn't you see me spit in it?

567
00:43:33,093 --> 00:43:36,014
You're my brother. What's the matter?
It's not like you have a disease.

568
00:43:40,016 --> 00:43:43,148
Fine, you guys eat it all.
I'll just make another batch.

569
00:43:53,060 --> 00:43:55,126
Why are there only four packs left?

570
00:43:55,700 --> 00:43:58,694
I want ramen too. Save me some.

571
00:43:58,922 --> 00:44:00,314
Gyu Min.

572
00:44:03,493 --> 00:44:04,898
It's good.

573
00:44:08,579 --> 00:44:10,404
Me too. Give me some first.

574
00:44:12,787 --> 00:44:16,824
- Dad, you like uncooked ramen too, right?
- What?

575
00:44:18,353 --> 00:44:23,216
Dad, hurry and crush these up
and eat them before Gyu Rim cooks them.

576
00:44:25,080 --> 00:44:26,792
Gyu Rim is making ramen?

577
00:44:27,979 --> 00:44:29,859
- Four whole packs?
- Yeah.

578
00:44:30,185 --> 00:44:32,912
There were only four packs left at home.

579
00:44:33,373 --> 00:44:37,419
Anyway, Gyu O and Gyu Seo are eating
the first seven packs she made,

580
00:44:37,967 --> 00:44:40,322
and I need to join them before they burst.

581
00:44:40,473 --> 00:44:43,947
Dad, eat all of these. Okay? Hurry!

582
00:44:47,347 --> 00:44:50,440
- She made seven packs of ramen?
- What?

583
00:44:51,014 --> 00:44:55,346
What do you mean Gyu Rim made
seven packs of ramen this morning?

584
00:44:55,647 --> 00:44:58,487
Gyu Rim doesn't even like ramen that much.

585
00:44:58,892 --> 00:45:04,278
Two years ago, Gyu O, Gyu Seo,
Gyu Yeong, and I...

586
00:45:05,319 --> 00:45:09,705
The four of us really upset her
all at once.

587
00:45:10,814 --> 00:45:13,828
Back then, Gyu Rim made five packs
and ate them all by herself.

588
00:45:14,007 --> 00:45:18,092
What? Five packs of ramen by herself?

589
00:45:19,147 --> 00:45:21,699
It's not like Gyu Rim is Tzuyang.

590
00:45:21,807 --> 00:45:23,799
Didn't she burst after eating all that?

591
00:45:24,507 --> 00:45:29,424
She didn't burst, but she got indigestion,
threw up, and had a really hard time.

592
00:45:30,287 --> 00:45:32,990
I thought she was going to die back then.

593
00:45:34,687 --> 00:45:35,936
Really?

594
00:45:56,013 --> 00:45:58,453
Hey, eat slowly. And take some antacid.

595
00:45:58,753 --> 00:46:01,390
So you can eat it all
while I'm getting the medicine?

596
00:46:01,907 --> 00:46:04,696
You slow down too. Aren't you on a diet?

597
00:46:05,273 --> 00:46:07,439
Gyu O must've eaten three packs
by himself.

598
00:46:07,526 --> 00:46:09,510
Why are you swallowing the ramen whole?

599
00:46:09,535 --> 00:46:11,257
Gyu O, take some antacid.

600
00:46:13,512 --> 00:46:15,154
- Hey, give me some more.
- It's okay.

601
00:46:15,179 --> 00:46:17,434
I'll eat it all.

602
00:46:17,459 --> 00:46:19,189
Hey, there's more here.

603
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:21,429
Come here. Hold out your bowl.

604
00:46:21,514 --> 00:46:23,357
That's so petty.

605
00:46:23,382 --> 00:46:26,663
Stop fighting, you brats. Bowls out.

606
00:46:40,280 --> 00:46:43,247
Take potatoes, for example.

607
00:46:44,398 --> 00:46:50,335
Even if a farmer plants the seeds,
waters them, and takes good care of them,

608
00:46:51,501 --> 00:46:56,335
not every potato turns out the same.
That's what my mom used to say.

609
00:46:57,480 --> 00:47:01,201
Some potatoes turn out well, like those,

610
00:47:02,140 --> 00:47:06,764
while others grow however they please,
like that defective potato.

611
00:47:11,893 --> 00:47:16,147
But even a defective potato
that grows however it pleases,

612
00:47:17,211 --> 00:47:23,142
knows how hard the farmer worked
through droughts and floods,

613
00:47:23,545 --> 00:47:30,503
and how much he worried over each potato.
That's what she used to say.

614
00:47:49,633 --> 00:47:51,695
Gyu Rim made seven packs of ramen.

615
00:47:53,086 --> 00:47:58,202
Go grab your chopsticks and help out,
you defective potato.

616
00:47:58,500 --> 00:48:01,968
It wasn't because of me.
It's because of Han Gyu O.

617
00:48:02,633 --> 00:48:06,153
Han Gyu O already started the trouble.
I barely lifted a finger.

618
00:48:06,178 --> 00:48:08,233
Lifted a finger, my foot!

619
00:48:08,500 --> 00:48:12,951
Because of you, Gyu Rim was almost hit
by Seong Uk's car, then kicked and beaten.

620
00:48:12,976 --> 00:48:14,364
What are you talking about?

621
00:48:17,660 --> 00:48:20,158
Kang Seong Uk, that jerk is asking for it!

622
00:48:24,921 --> 00:48:28,135
Mu Jin got plenty of revenge for Gyu Rim.

623
00:48:28,866 --> 00:48:31,587
He knocked out all
of Kang Seong Uk's teeth,

624
00:48:31,674 --> 00:48:35,101
broke bones all over his body,
and nearly killed him.

625
00:48:37,839 --> 00:48:40,874
- He's in the hospital right now, so...
- Which hospital?

626
00:48:41,508 --> 00:48:46,215
Mu Jin can handle his own revenge.
I'll handle mine.

627
00:48:46,587 --> 00:48:49,068
- I'm going to kill him.
- Hey.

628
00:48:51,046 --> 00:48:54,129
If you go off the rails too,

629
00:48:54,430 --> 00:48:57,510
your sister will have to cook
ten packs of ramen.

630
00:49:02,380 --> 00:49:04,705
You're a good girl after all...

631
00:49:07,333 --> 00:49:10,047
It must've been so hard for you
to pretend to be bad all this time.

632
00:49:29,967 --> 00:49:31,461
Hello?

633
00:49:31,949 --> 00:49:34,169
- Han Gyeol?
- Yes.

634
00:49:36,005 --> 00:49:37,900
Did I wake you up?

635
00:49:38,114 --> 00:49:43,415
No. I've been up for a while,
but I was too lazy to get up.

636
00:49:44,422 --> 00:49:46,682
But who is this?

637
00:49:47,114 --> 00:49:49,373
Well,

638
00:49:49,826 --> 00:49:56,420
I'm the grandma you told last time
about a great spicy rice cake place.

639
00:49:57,220 --> 00:50:00,895
I remember. Hello.

640
00:50:02,361 --> 00:50:09,155
I'm going to that spicy rice cake place
for lunch later,

641
00:50:09,561 --> 00:50:12,038
so would you like to join me?

642
00:50:12,567 --> 00:50:17,815
Mom told me not to go with strangers
who offer to buy me things.

643
00:50:20,625 --> 00:50:23,475
But I'm not a stranger.

644
00:50:26,680 --> 00:50:30,147
You know Mu Jin, right?

645
00:50:30,780 --> 00:50:35,440
I'm his mom.

646
00:50:35,839 --> 00:50:37,293
Really?

647
00:50:38,500 --> 00:50:41,600
Yes, why would I lie to you?

648
00:50:42,947 --> 00:50:44,954
But if you need proof,

649
00:50:44,979 --> 00:50:48,900
I'll send you a picture of me with Mu Jin.
Hold on.

650
00:50:53,562 --> 00:50:55,896
(Han Gyeol)

651
00:50:59,053 --> 00:51:02,789
Gyeol, keep this picture to yourself.
And one more thing...

652
00:51:02,936 --> 00:51:07,189
I'd like you to keep my call a secret
from your mom for a while.

653
00:51:07,589 --> 00:51:09,419
Can you do that?

654
00:51:12,294 --> 00:51:13,710
Yes, good.

655
00:51:13,963 --> 00:51:18,503
See you there, then. I'll be waiting.

656
00:51:30,467 --> 00:51:31,876
Good job, Mom.

657
00:51:32,413 --> 00:51:34,693
- You did so well.
- What's gotten into you?

658
00:51:34,718 --> 00:51:37,040
Hey, were you eavesdropping outside?

659
00:51:38,588 --> 00:51:42,645
If you're that curious,
why not just bug the place?

660
00:51:42,670 --> 00:51:45,505
Can I really? Am I allowed to bug you?

661
00:51:47,911 --> 00:51:50,430
- Good job, Mom.
- Go away.

662
00:51:50,455 --> 00:51:52,660
- Now you finally feel like my mom.
- Go away.

663
00:51:53,974 --> 00:51:57,274
Yes. So what's the current situation?

664
00:51:57,473 --> 00:52:02,570
Kang Sang Man and Sim Su Ji were arrested
for fraud, extortion, and intimidation.

665
00:52:02,699 --> 00:52:06,102
Since they have prior similar convictions
and are considered a flight risk,

666
00:52:06,223 --> 00:52:08,569
they'll stand trial in custody.

667
00:52:08,745 --> 00:52:09,907
Good.

668
00:52:10,127 --> 00:52:16,622
As I reported last night, Kang Seong Uk
was charged with assaulting Han Gyu Rim,

669
00:52:16,647 --> 00:52:19,082
and a hit-and-run,
and will be brought to trial.

670
00:52:19,313 --> 00:52:24,791
Can you move faster
on Gyu Yeong's divorce?

671
00:52:25,123 --> 00:52:28,296
Yes. Since it's tied to a criminal case,

672
00:52:28,483 --> 00:52:32,351
Kang Seong Uk's side has decided
there's nothing to gain by holding out,

673
00:52:32,739 --> 00:52:35,739
so it looks like they'll reach
an uncontested divorce agreement.

674
00:52:36,279 --> 00:52:39,876
If it goes quickly,
it should be wrapped up in about a month.

675
00:52:40,327 --> 00:52:44,334
I see. Please keep working on it
until it's settled.

676
00:52:44,607 --> 00:52:50,996
Attorney Kim, make sure Gyu Yeong
doesn't find out I'm involved. Understood?

677
00:52:51,021 --> 00:52:52,578
Yes, understood.

678
00:52:52,864 --> 00:52:54,040
Excuse me a moment.

679
00:52:55,086 --> 00:52:57,039
(Gyu Yeong)

680
00:52:58,814 --> 00:53:01,210
- That's all, right?
- Yes.

681
00:53:01,235 --> 00:53:03,496
- Thank you for your work.
- Yes.

682
00:53:03,521 --> 00:53:04,850
- Good work.
- Thanks.

683
00:53:04,875 --> 00:53:06,467
- Thank you.
- Of course.

684
00:53:08,737 --> 00:53:09,840
Hello.

685
00:53:12,738 --> 00:53:13,866
Really?

686
00:53:16,194 --> 00:53:19,042
Then let's meet
at the office in 30 minutes.

687
00:53:19,610 --> 00:53:20,637
Okay.

688
00:53:25,151 --> 00:53:29,781
- Secretary Jeong, don't let anyone in.
- Yes, understood.

689
00:53:29,839 --> 00:53:30,861
Go ahead.

690
00:53:37,380 --> 00:53:41,806
My divorce is going to work out fine,
even without your help, sir.

691
00:53:43,878 --> 00:53:45,087
That's good.

692
00:53:48,334 --> 00:53:54,242
Sorry, I took your kindness for granted
and acted out without knowing my place.

693
00:54:01,380 --> 00:54:04,131
I told you not to let anyone in. Didn't I?

694
00:54:08,225 --> 00:54:09,254
Seo Hyeon, what is it?

695
00:54:13,320 --> 00:54:15,287
Didn't you see me in the elevator?

696
00:54:16,969 --> 00:54:18,209
No, I didn't.

697
00:54:18,660 --> 00:54:20,486
We made eye contact.

698
00:54:20,629 --> 00:54:22,887
I tried to say hi,
but you just ignored me and walked away.

699
00:54:22,912 --> 00:54:23,941
Seo Hyeon.

700
00:54:25,567 --> 00:54:27,526
So I'm supposed to acknowledge you
in front of everyone at work?

701
00:54:27,854 --> 00:54:29,309
You're the daughter my mom raised, right?

702
00:54:29,334 --> 00:54:32,196
And I'm the daughter she gave birth to.
Should I make a big show of knowing you?

703
00:54:32,420 --> 00:54:35,029
Hey, how old are you?

704
00:54:35,054 --> 00:54:37,606
You're a whole year younger than me.
How dare you talk back to me?

705
00:54:37,660 --> 00:54:38,854
Jang Seo Hyeon.

706
00:54:45,540 --> 00:54:50,321
I don't know how long your power and money
will keep you on top, sir,

707
00:54:50,709 --> 00:54:53,042
but I'm Han Gyu Yeong,
and I won't go down like this.

708
00:54:53,999 --> 00:54:56,965
- What is she saying to you, Dad?
- Seo Hyeon.

709
00:54:59,467 --> 00:55:01,159
Yes, go on.

710
00:55:03,040 --> 00:55:08,083
Whether by elevator or by ladder,
I'll climb my way up to where you are.

711
00:55:08,312 --> 00:55:12,201
For all the pain you've caused me,
for all the tears I've shed,

712
00:55:12,368 --> 00:55:14,242
I'll pay you back for every bit of it.

713
00:55:15,134 --> 00:55:18,336
I'll make sure
you regret it as much as I did.

714
00:55:19,060 --> 00:55:20,944
I came to tell you that.

715
00:55:20,969 --> 00:55:25,258
Who do you think you're talking to?

716
00:55:25,283 --> 00:55:27,018
Stay out of this.

717
00:55:30,387 --> 00:55:31,432
All right.

718
00:55:33,346 --> 00:55:37,846
Then make me regret it.
Make me shed tears of blood.

719
00:55:38,154 --> 00:55:40,964
I'll be looking forward to it.

720
00:55:49,824 --> 00:55:52,894
Looking forward to what?

721
00:55:52,934 --> 00:55:55,376
Why would you even entertain
a crazy girl like her?

722
00:55:55,461 --> 00:55:58,144
Dad, I really don't understand you.
You're acting so weird. You know that?

723
00:56:00,347 --> 00:56:02,944
Hey, I'm hungry.
You haven't had lunch, right?

724
00:56:03,214 --> 00:56:05,547
Let's get bone soup, okay? Come on.

725
00:56:12,300 --> 00:56:14,620
They say the apple doesn't fall far
from the tree...

726
00:56:15,680 --> 00:56:19,409
- The tree?
- What? Nothing.

727
00:56:21,380 --> 00:56:23,836
- Thanks for the meal.
- Sure.

728
00:56:32,247 --> 00:56:33,688
- Can I ask something?
- Sure.

729
00:56:33,713 --> 00:56:37,261
Why didn't you tell me last time
that you were Mu Jin's mom?

730
00:56:37,788 --> 00:56:38,873
What?

731
00:56:40,506 --> 00:56:42,452
Last time?

732
00:56:43,692 --> 00:56:50,073
Back then, I hadn't given my blessing
to your mom and Mu Jin yet.

733
00:56:52,353 --> 00:56:56,653
Anyway, it's a long story.

734
00:56:58,348 --> 00:57:02,016
These spicy rice cakes are good. Eat up.

735
00:57:04,175 --> 00:57:05,827
Is it because I'm a burden?

736
00:57:08,097 --> 00:57:09,320
What?

737
00:57:09,874 --> 00:57:14,024
Is that why you didn't approve?
Because I'm a burden?

738
00:57:16,293 --> 00:57:20,283
No, that's not it.

739
00:57:20,827 --> 00:57:25,527
Why would you be a burden?
You're not a burden. You're a blessing.

740
00:57:28,840 --> 00:57:31,044
You're a little bundle of joy, Gyeol.

741
00:57:31,292 --> 00:57:37,014
That's why I'm trying to get
your mom and Mu Jin married.

742
00:57:39,286 --> 00:57:41,774
Don't cry.

743
00:57:41,946 --> 00:57:43,254
Don't cry.

744
00:57:44,522 --> 00:57:47,281
I'm sorry.

745
00:57:47,641 --> 00:57:50,840
It's okay. Eat. What do you want?
More spicy rice cakes?

746
00:57:51,006 --> 00:57:53,636
Want this? A rice roll?

747
00:57:54,427 --> 00:57:56,436
You're saying you're
Gyeol's biological father?

748
00:57:58,606 --> 00:58:02,218
Yes. I'm Gyeol's biological father.

749
00:58:10,580 --> 00:58:13,146
Talk about a bolt from the blue.

750
00:58:14,867 --> 00:58:17,369
Showing up out of nowhere
with something like this...

751
00:58:18,708 --> 00:58:20,855
This is ridiculous.

752
00:58:21,726 --> 00:58:23,498
Gyu Rim, Hye Jeong, and I...

753
00:58:24,786 --> 00:58:29,466
All three of us, his birth mom included,
were elementary school classmates.

754
00:58:32,020 --> 00:58:37,147
I contacted Gyeol's biological mother
and confirmed she left Gyeol with Gyu Rim.

755
00:58:46,079 --> 00:58:47,227
Gyeol...

756
00:58:50,187 --> 00:58:53,287
isn't a child I gave birth to.

757
00:58:57,927 --> 00:58:59,701
He's my friend's son.

758
00:59:02,274 --> 00:59:04,426
My friend couldn't raise him,

759
00:59:06,820 --> 00:59:10,066
so I raised him. My Gyeol.

760
00:59:13,393 --> 00:59:15,872
I also checked the hospital records
from the day Gyeol was born.

761
00:59:20,827 --> 00:59:23,218
I confirmed that Gyu Rim's baby
was stillborn.

762
00:59:26,187 --> 00:59:33,146
I guess a little one from the sky
lost its way for a while.

763
00:59:36,300 --> 00:59:38,137
The moment it came into the world...

764
00:59:42,219 --> 00:59:45,326
it went back to the sky.

765
00:59:49,526 --> 00:59:50,900
I'm going to use the restroom.

766
00:59:52,100 --> 00:59:54,041
I've already done a DNA test too.

767
01:00:01,367 --> 01:00:02,417
What?

768
01:00:03,480 --> 01:00:06,936
I didn't meet him.
I used a strand of hair he'd left behind.

769
01:00:08,627 --> 01:00:12,154
I wanted to be certain,
not just make an assumption. So...

770
01:00:14,220 --> 01:00:16,339
I could make a decision.

771
01:00:18,721 --> 01:00:20,061
A decision?

772
01:00:21,363 --> 01:00:22,917
What kind of decision?

773
01:00:31,636 --> 01:00:35,830
(Suragan Side Dishes)

774
01:01:06,585 --> 01:01:08,174
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

775
01:01:17,986 --> 01:01:19,782
I was wrong.

776
01:01:26,299 --> 01:01:27,629
I'm sorry.

777
01:01:29,860 --> 01:01:31,822
I'm so sorry.

778
01:01:42,521 --> 01:01:44,307
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

779
01:01:46,363 --> 01:01:47,699
I'm sorry.

780
01:01:55,106 --> 01:01:56,750
That feels so good.

781
01:01:57,947 --> 01:02:00,860
Who are you to keep calling me Mom?

782
01:02:01,581 --> 01:02:04,946
I've never had a son like you.

783
01:02:06,081 --> 01:02:07,441
Enough. I'm hanging up.

784
01:02:09,453 --> 01:02:12,992
You'd sell your own mother
for a quick buck!

785
01:02:14,961 --> 01:02:20,981
I can't believe I gave birth to such trash
and even ate seaweed soup!

786
01:02:25,833 --> 01:02:27,467
What, are you renting this spot?

787
01:02:27,987 --> 01:02:29,554
Shouldn't you be working at the store?

788
01:02:31,347 --> 01:02:35,661
I set it up so my phone rings
whenever a customer comes in.

789
01:02:35,773 --> 01:02:40,877
I'd normally let you have the space,
but I'm under so much stress myself.

790
01:02:41,087 --> 01:02:46,069
I need to lie down for at least 30 minutes
to unwind from work.

791
01:02:53,066 --> 01:02:57,513
Go ahead. If you're stressed,
let it all out here.

792
01:02:57,914 --> 01:03:02,329
That way, you won't take it out
on poor Gyu Rim.

793
01:03:05,234 --> 01:03:07,174
Who's that woman?

794
01:03:07,953 --> 01:03:10,332
Isn't that Gyu Rim's mother?

795
01:03:14,040 --> 01:03:15,122
Who?

796
01:03:15,647 --> 01:03:19,359
Why is she kneeling
on the ground like that?

797
01:03:20,881 --> 01:03:22,314
What's going on?

798
01:03:30,607 --> 01:03:33,342
So you really did have an ulterior motive.

799
01:03:33,880 --> 01:03:37,436
You wanted Seok Jung back, didn't you?

800
01:03:38,581 --> 01:03:43,303
Now that I want him back,
you're jealous all over again.

801
01:03:43,593 --> 01:03:47,769
Because Seok Jung's such a catch.

802
01:03:50,194 --> 01:03:53,579
Go. Just go!

803
01:03:54,347 --> 01:03:58,675
You can't just come back
because you want to. So leave!

804
01:04:00,920 --> 01:04:04,621
Go. I said go!

805
01:04:05,933 --> 01:04:07,473
Don't touch her.

806
01:04:08,514 --> 01:04:10,721
Don't you touch my mom.

807
01:04:11,567 --> 01:04:14,021
Who are you to lay a hand on my mom?

808
01:04:15,227 --> 01:04:17,951
I said don't touch my mom!

809
01:04:50,494 --> 01:04:52,594
(Love on the Menu)

810
01:04:52,619 --> 01:04:54,702
Do you happen to like me?

811
01:04:54,827 --> 01:04:57,137
You're the first one ever.

812
01:04:57,162 --> 01:04:58,981
I have an eight-year-old son.

813
01:04:59,006 --> 01:05:00,301
What do you mean by that?

814
01:05:00,326 --> 01:05:02,151
Can't you just let go and leave?

815
01:05:02,176 --> 01:05:05,081
People might start thinking you're my dad.

816
01:05:05,173 --> 01:05:06,660
Hey, I'm as good as your dad.

817
01:05:06,685 --> 01:05:07,722
Let's move abroad.

818
01:05:07,747 --> 01:05:08,907
Is something wrong?

819
01:05:08,932 --> 01:05:10,072
I won't let you take Gyeol.

820
01:05:10,167 --> 01:05:12,407
- I'll even sue if I have to.
- What?

821
01:05:12,432 --> 01:05:15,077
- Han Gyeol.
- Blood is blood.

822
01:05:15,102 --> 01:05:17,485
Blood is thicker than water.

823
01:05:17,510 --> 01:05:18,745
Who are you?

824
01:05:20,536 --> 01:05:22,336
Dramaday.me
